WEBVTT

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.380
He wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.430
Saving people,hunting
things. The family business.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.130
Today's your lucky day,kid.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.030
You watch out for sammy,okay?
Yeah,dad. You know I will.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.040
Dad.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.560
Time of death -10:41 A.M.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.990
I miss him,man,and I'm not
all right. Neither are you.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.970
I'm dealing with dad's death!

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.650
Dad's dead,and it hurts
so bad, you can't take it.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.370
I'm okay! I swear,the next
person who asks if I'm okay,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.280
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.210
Okay,we got booze...

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.420
We got chocolate...

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.020
And...wait for it.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.650
Tortured emo rock.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.840
Guaranteed cure for any broken heart.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.080
You didn't have to do all this.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.700
I'm fine.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.470
Yeah,I can see that.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.610
Thanks,neal.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.890
You're a good friend.

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.300
It's probably him.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.410
I'll take care of it.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:34.700
Where is she?

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.810
Chill out and think about this,okay?

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.330
I need to talk to her. Some other time.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.570
You get out of my face now.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.280
Angela?

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.960
Leave...me...alone.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.730
Angela,I'm sorry.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.930
You're sorry?

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.190
You're sorry? Oh,that's great.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.540
Angela,listen to me.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.140
I don't want to listen to you!

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.890
I'm done listening! Listen to me.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.880
How could you do this? I loved you.

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.290
Angela?

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.030
Angela!

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.660
Come on,sam. I'm begging
you. This is stupid.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.700
Why?

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.870
Going to visit mom's grave?

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.130
She doesn't even have a grave. There
was no body left after the fire.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:14.290
She has a headstone.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.500
Put up by our uncle, a
man that we've never met.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.980
You want to pay your respects to a
slab of granite put up by a stranger.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.460
That's not the point. Then enlighten me.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.450
It's not about a body or a casket.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.250
It's about her memory, okay?

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.850
And after
dad,it just --

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.580
It just feels like
the right thing to do.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.030
It's irrational is what it is.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.650
Look,man, no one asked you to come.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.340
Why don't we swing by
the roadhouse instead?

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:41.190
We haven't heard anything on the demon lately.
We should be hunting that son of a bitch down.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.780
That's a good idea. You should.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.050
Just drop me off,I'll hitch a ride,
and I'll meet you there tomorrow.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.940
Right.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:53.360
Stuck with those people, making
awkward small talk until you show up.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.160
No,thanks.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:29.400
I think,uh...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.190
I think dad would have
wanted you to have these.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:48.650
I love you,mom.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.100
Thank you.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.500
Angela mason.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.600
She was a student at the local
college. Her funeral was three days ago.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.280
And?

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:20.660
And?

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.210
You saw her grave -- Everything
dead around it in a perfect circle.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.540
You don't think that's a little weird?

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.730
Maybe the grounds keeper went a
little agro with the pesticide.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:31.730
No,I asked him. No pesticide,no
chemicals. Nobody can explain it.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.490
Okay, so,what are you thinking?

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.050
I don't know. Unholy ground,maybe.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.890
What?

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:42.830
If something evil happened,it
could easily poison the ground.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.230
Remember the farm
outside of cedar rapids?

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:45.930
Yeah.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:49.020
It could be the sign
of a demonic presence

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.820
Or the angela girl's spirit,
if it's powerful enough.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.760
Well,don't get too excited.
You might pull something.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.890
It's just stumbling onto a hunt...

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.750
Here of all places? So?

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.270
So,are you sure this is about
a hunt,not something else?

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:08.740
What else would it be about?

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.850
Just forget it.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:12.900
Believe what you want,sam,

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:17.020
But I let you drag my ass out here.
The least we can do is check this out.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:21.410
Yeah,fine.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.420
The girl's dad works in town.
He's a professor at the school.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:41.810
Dr. Mason? Yes.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.350
I'm sam. This is dean.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:46.400
We were friends of angela'S.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:50.020
We -We wanted to offer our condolences.

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.420
Please come in.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.520
She was beautiful.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.600
Yes,she was.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.420
This is an unusual book.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.690
It's ancient greek. I teach a course.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:26.100
So,a car accident.
That's -That's horrible.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:29.960
Angie was only a mile
away from home when...

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:35.980
It's got to be hard...
losing someone like that.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:40.300
Sometimes it's like
they're still around,

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:44.510
Almost like you can still
sense their presence.

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:46.280
You ever feel anything like that?

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:49.110
I do,as a matter of fact.

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.970
That's perfectly normal, dr. Mason,

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:57.290
Especially with what
you're going through.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:01.140
You know, I still phone her.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:05.430
And the phone's ringing
before I remember that,uh...

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.800
Family's everything, you know?

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.010
Angie was the most
important thing in my life.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.900
And now I'm just lost without her.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:27.020
I'm very sorry.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:31.070
There's something going on.
We just haven't found it yet.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:35.560
Dean,so far you got a patch
of dead grass and nothing.

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.800
Well,something turned that
grave into unholy ground.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.350
There's no reason for
it to be unholy ground.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:42.660
Angela mason was a nice
girl who died in a car crash.

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:45.100
That's not exactly
vengeful-Spirit material.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.660
You heard her father.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:50.450
Maybe daddy doesn't know  everything
there is to know about his little angel,

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:53.750
You know what? We never should
have bothered that poor man.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.490
We shouldn't even be here anymore.

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:59.560
So,what,sam?We just bail without
even figuring out what's going on?

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:02.720
I think I know what's going on here.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:05.400
It's the only reason I went
along with you this far.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.610
What are you talking about?
This is about mom's grave.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.710
Got nothing to do with it.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.830
You wouldn't step
within 100 yards of it.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:18.410
Look,maybe you're imagining
a hunt where there isn't one

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:22.250
So you don't have to
think about mom or dad.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:34.160
You want to take another swing? Go ahead

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.650
If it will make you feel better.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.140
I don't need this crap.

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:46.040
Dean,where are you going?

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.710
I'm gonna go get a drink...

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.630
Alone.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.510
Who the hell are you?!
Wait,wait,wait,wait.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:47.000
Hold on!

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.540
I'm calling 911!

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.090
'M angela's cousin. What?

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.380
Yeah,her dad sent me
over to pick up her stuff.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:57.710
My name's alan
-- Alan stanwick.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:03.830
Her dad didn't say that you were coming.

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.760
Well,I mean...

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.840
How else would I have
the key to your place?

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:26.490
So,I'm sure you got a view of angela
that none of the family got to see.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.560
Tell me,what was she like?

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.160
What was she really like?

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.150
She was great...

00:13:32.150 --> 00:13:35.610
Just...great.

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:38.190
I mean,she was so...

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:41.940
Great.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.390
Yeah.

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:47.230
Yeah.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:53.540
You two must have been really close,huh?

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.020
We were.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.580
But it's not just her, it's matt.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.560
Who?

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.160
Angela's boyfriend.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.260
Right -Matt.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.110
Uh,what about him?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.640
He killed himself last night.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:12.900
He cut his own throat. Who does that?

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:16.190
That'S...terrible.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:20.350
He was taking angela's death
pretty hard,and I guess...

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:25.240
I mean,he'd been messed
up about it for days.

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.480
Messed up how?

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:29.370
He kept saying that
he saw her everywhere.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:31.290
Well,I'm -- I'm
sure that's normal.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.250
I mean,with everything
he was going through.

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.960
He said that he saw her...

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:39.120
As in an acid trip or something.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.580
Were angela and matt a happy couple?

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:45.340
I mean,was there any reason that
angela would be angry with him?

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.120
What?

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.880
No,of course not. Why do you ask?

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:52.960
Just asking.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.680
Where did matt live?

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:58.610
Next on cinemax,

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:00.710
"Casa erotica iv,"

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.730
A tale of two latin beauties,

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.910
Hey.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:11.280
What?

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.160
Awkward.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:15.950
Where the hell were you? Just
working my imaginary case.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:19.050
Yeah? And?

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.840
Oh,well,you were right.
I didn't find much.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:24.770
Yeah. Except angela's
boyfriend died last night --

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.380
Slit his own throat,
but,you know,that's normal.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:28.720
Uh,let's see. What else?

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:32.550
Oh,he was seeing angela
everywhere before he died.

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.880
But,you know,I'm sure  that's just
me transferring my own feelings.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.430
Okay,I get it.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.260
I'm sorry. Maybe there is
something going on here.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:40.910
Maybe?

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.910
Sam,I know how to do my job
despite what you might think.

00:15:46.450 --> 00:15:48.790
We should check out the guy's apartment.

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.350
I just came from there...

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.280
A pile of dead plants
just like the cemetery.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.040
Hell,a dead goldfish,too.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.730
So,unholy ground? Maybe.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:02.710
I'm still not getting that powerful
angry-Spirit vibe from angela.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.280
I've been reading this, though.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:13.550
You stole the girl's diary? Yeah,sam.

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.900
And if anything, the
girl's a little too nice.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:18.320
So,what do you want to do?

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.110
Keep digging, talk to
more of her friends.

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:22.640
You get any names? You kidding me?

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:26.020
I have her bestest friend
in the whole wide world.

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:30.620
I didn't realize the college
employed grief counselors.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:31.810
Oh,yeah.

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:33.520
Yeah,you talk,we listen

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.630
And maybe throw in a little therapeutic
collage whatever helps jump-Start the healing.

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:40.910
Well,I think I'm okay. Thanks.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:43.850
Well,you heard what happened
to matt harrison,right?

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.230
Yeah,I did.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.980
We just wanted to make
sure you were okay.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:51.380
Grief can make people do crazy things.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.720
Look,I'm sorry about
what happened to him.I am.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.690
But if matt killed himself,
it wasn't 'cause of grief.

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.390
No? Then why?

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:03.420
It was guilt.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:05.770
Angie's death was matt's
fault, and he knew it.

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:07.620
How was matt responsible?

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:10.040
She really loved that guy,

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:13.620
But the night of the accident, she
walked in on him with another girl.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.900
She was really torn up.
That's why she crashed.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.370
Um,look, I got to get ready for work,

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:27.790
So thanks for the concern,
but,seriously,I'll be okay.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:35.680
Well,my vengeful-Spirit theory is
starting to make a little more sense.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.280
I mean,hell hath no fury.

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:42.350
So,if angela got her revenge
on matt,you think it's over?

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:45.790
Well, there's one way to be sure.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.740
Yeah? What's that?

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.750
Burn the bones.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.810
Burn the bones?

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:57.890
Are you high? Angela died last week.

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.250
So?

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:03.840
So there's not gonna be bones. There's
gonna be a ripe,rotting body in the coffin.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.810
Since when are you
afraid to get dirty,huh?

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.490
Ladies first.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:39.440
Hold that.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:17.670
I missed you.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.150
They buried the body four days ago.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:44.620
I don't get it.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.210
Look.

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:52.090
What is that? I'm not sure.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.160
I've seen these kinds of symbols before.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:01.040
Dean,take it easy,okay?

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:09.820
You're angie's friends.

00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:12.350
Dr. Mason --
We need to talk.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:14.890
Well,come in.

00:20:15.870 --> 00:20:17.370
Thanks.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.620
You teach ancient greek.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.640
Tell me...

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:27.100
What are these?

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.630
I don't understand.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:33.370
You said this had
something to do with angela.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:36.500
It does. Please,just humor me.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:41.470
They're part of an ancient
greek divination ritual.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.990
Used for necromancy,right. That's right.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.110
See, before we came over here,

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:48.290
We stopped by the library and
did a little homework ourselves.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:52.430
Apparently, they use rituals like this
one for communicating with the dead,

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:56.320
Even bringing corpses back to
life -Full-On zombie action.

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.230
Yeah.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:01.490
I mean, according to the legends.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.450
Now,what's this all about?

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.510
I think you know. Dean.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:08.540
Look,I get it.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.740
There are people that I would
give anything to see again,

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:12.910
But what gives you the right?

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.160
Dean. What are you talking about?

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.720
What's dead should stay dead! What?

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:18.180
Stop it! What you brought
back isn't your daughter!

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:20.700
These things are
vicious, they're violent!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.850
They're so nasty, they
rot the ground around them.

00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:25.540
I mean,come on! Haven't
you seen "pet sematary"?

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.150
You're insane.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:31.380
Where is she? Get out of my house.

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:33.650
I know you're hiding her
somewhere. Where is she?!

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:35.960
Dean,stop! That's
enough. Dean,look --

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:40.180
Beautiful,living plants. We're leaving.

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:42.350
I'm calling the police. Sir,we're sorry.

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:45.010
We won't bother you again.

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:50.040
What the hell's the
matter with you? Back off.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.380
That man is innocent.
He didn't deserve that.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:54.640
So she's not here. Maybe he's
keeping her somewhere else.

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:56.800
Stop it! That's enough,okay? Enough!

00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:59.150
Sam,I know what I'm doing.
No,you don'T...at all.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:02.670
I don't scare easy,but you're
scaring the crap out of me.

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:04.140
Don't be overdramatic, sam.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:06.090
You're lucky this turned
out to be a real case,

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:09.180
'Cause if it wasn't,you would've
found something else to kill.

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:11.070
You're on edge, you're erratic,

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:13.880
Except for when you're hunting,'cause
then you're downright scary.

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:15.870
You're tailspinning,man,

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:19.380
And you refuse to talk about it,
and you won't let me help you.

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:20.870
I can take care of myself, thanks.

00:22:20.870 --> 00:22:22.750
No,you can't!

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:26.020
And you're the only one who
thinks you should have to.

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:28.420
You don't have to handle
this on your own. No one can.

00:22:28.420 --> 00:22:32.170
If you bring up dad's death one more
time -- Dean,it's killing you. Please.

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:37.360
We've already lost dad.

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:39.200
We lost mom.

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:42.230
I've lost jessica.

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:45.190
And now I'm gonna lose you,too?

00:22:46.910 --> 00:22:49.580
We better get out of
here before the cops come.

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.190
I hear you,okay?

00:22:53.190 --> 00:22:55.920
I'm being an ass, and I'm sorry.

00:22:55.920 --> 00:22:59.660
But we got a freakin' zombie running
around. We need to figure out how to kill it.

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:04.400
Right?

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:06.820
Our lives are weird,man.

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:09.100
You're telling me.

00:23:10.050 --> 00:23:12.650
Come on.

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:16.720
Honey, is something bothering you?

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:20.140
It's about matt.

00:23:20.140 --> 00:23:21.990
Haven't we already talked about that?

00:23:21.990 --> 00:23:23.190
I
know,but,uh --

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:26.750
Haven't we wasted enough
time on him already?

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:30.460
Come sit down.

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:41.000
You always said that
he didn't deserve me.

00:23:41.610 --> 00:23:44.250
You were right. Angela...

00:23:46.680 --> 00:23:50.430
You didn't get out and go see matt or...

00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:52.610
I've been here the whole time.

00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:58.870
Neal...you really think I
could do something like that?

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.580
No,I... I don't know.

00:24:02.320 --> 00:24:05.130
I can't help it. You just -You seem...

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:07.000
Different?

00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:10.990
You're right. I am.

00:24:13.650 --> 00:24:16.380
I've realized...

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:19.940
You're the only one who
ever really loved me.

00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:26.410
You proved that. You brought me back.

00:24:26.410 --> 00:24:28.910
I'm with you now.

00:24:29.750 --> 00:24:33.050
Isn't that what you always wanted?

00:24:36.080 --> 00:24:38.340
We can't just waste
her with a head shot?

00:24:38.340 --> 00:24:41.160
Dude,you've been wahing
way too many romero flicks.

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:43.260
You're telling me there's
no lore on how to smoke them?

00:24:43.260 --> 00:24:45.580
No,I'm telling you there's too much.

00:24:45.580 --> 00:24:47.660
There's 100 different
legends on the walking dead,

00:24:47.660 --> 00:24:49.560
But they all have different
methods for killing them.

00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:53.980
Some say setting them on
fire. One said -Where is it?

00:24:53.980 --> 00:24:56.340
Right here -Feeding
their hearts to wild dogs.

00:24:56.340 --> 00:24:58.170
That's my personal favorite.

00:24:58.170 --> 00:24:59.830
But who knows what's
real and what's myth?

00:24:59.830 --> 00:25:01.410
Is there anything they have in common?

00:25:01.410 --> 00:25:03.640
No,but a few said silver might work.

00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:05.130
Silver's a start.

00:25:05.130 --> 00:25:06.860
But now how are we going to find angela?

00:25:06.860 --> 00:25:08.540
We got to figure out
who brought her back.

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:10.160
Any ideas?

00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:13.210
I think if it's not her dad,
it might be that guy,neal.

00:25:13.210 --> 00:25:14.610
Neal? Yep.

00:25:14.610 --> 00:25:17.380
How'd you come up with that?
Well,you got your journal,I got mine.

00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:20.190
"Neal's a real shoulder to cry on.

00:25:20.190 --> 00:25:23.980
He so understands what I'm
going through with matt."

00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:28.070
There's more here where that came from. It's
got unrequited duckie love written all over it.

00:25:28.070 --> 00:25:30.550
But that doesn't mean he
brought her back from the dead.

00:25:30.550 --> 00:25:33.080
Hmm,did I mention that
he's professor mason's T.A.?

00:25:33.080 --> 00:25:36.010
Has access to all the same books.

00:25:41.450 --> 00:25:43.250
Hello?

00:25:46.730 --> 00:25:48.750
Neal!

00:25:49.390 --> 00:25:52.150
It's your grief counselors.
We've come to hug.

00:25:55.720 --> 00:25:57.180
Silver bullets?

00:25:57.180 --> 00:26:00.380
Yeah,enough to make her
rattle like a change purse.

00:26:26.630 --> 00:26:29.030
Unless it's where he keeps his porn.

00:26:56.900 --> 00:26:59.440
It sure looks like a zombie pen to me.

00:26:59.440 --> 00:27:00.850
Yeah.

00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:03.390
An empty one.

00:27:04.830 --> 00:27:07.750
You think angela's gone after somebody?

00:27:17.180 --> 00:27:19.240
No,I think she went
out to rent "beaches."

00:27:19.240 --> 00:27:22.310
Look,smartass. She might kill someone.

00:27:22.310 --> 00:27:24.550
We got to find her,dean.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:27.170
Yeah.

00:27:27.730 --> 00:27:30.710
All right,she clipped matt
because he was cheating,right?

00:27:30.710 --> 00:27:31.710
Yeah.

00:27:31.710 --> 00:27:36.480
Well,takes two to,you
know, have hard-Core sex.

00:27:37.360 --> 00:27:38.420
I don't know. It just seemed

00:27:38.420 --> 00:27:40.950
That angela's roommate was...

00:27:40.950 --> 00:27:44.090
Broken up over matt's death.

00:27:44.530 --> 00:27:48.850
I mean, like really broken up.

00:28:06.830 --> 00:28:09.000
Hello?

00:28:16.730 --> 00:28:18.820
Hi,lindsay. I'm home.

00:28:28.010 --> 00:28:30.000
You know what you did.

00:28:32.820 --> 00:28:33.970
I'm sorry!

00:28:33.970 --> 00:28:35.560
I am so sorry!

00:28:35.560 --> 00:28:37.380
Not sorry enough!

00:28:59.950 --> 00:29:01.120
God.

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:04.490
God.

00:29:04.490 --> 00:29:05.960
Oh,my god.

00:29:05.960 --> 00:29:07.220
Oh,my god.

00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:39.220
I got you. I got you.

00:29:42.390 --> 00:29:44.460
Damn, that dead chick can run.

00:29:44.460 --> 00:29:46.700
What now?

00:29:47.200 --> 00:29:49.620
I say we go have a
little chat with neal.

00:29:53.320 --> 00:29:56.330
So,the silver bullets,
they did something,right?

00:29:56.330 --> 00:29:59.810
Yeah,something,but not
enough. What else you got?

00:30:00.910 --> 00:30:02.380
Um,okay,besides silver,

00:30:02.380 --> 00:30:05.850
We have "nailing the undead
back into their grave beds."

00:30:05.850 --> 00:30:10.210
It's mentioned a few times. It's probably
where the whole vampire-Staking lore came from.

00:30:10.210 --> 00:30:12.410
Their grave beds? You serious?

00:30:12.410 --> 00:30:13.440
Yeah.

00:30:13.440 --> 00:30:16.650
How the hell are we gonna get
angela back to the cemetery?

00:30:28.140 --> 00:30:30.120
What are you guys doing here?

00:30:31.750 --> 00:30:34.890
You know,I've heard of some people doing
some pretty desperate things to get laid,

00:30:34.890 --> 00:30:36.610
But you

00:30:36.610 --> 00:30:38.790
You take the cake.

00:30:38.790 --> 00:30:40.380
Okay,who are you guys?

00:30:40.380 --> 00:30:42.730
You might want to ask
angela that question.

00:30:42.730 --> 00:30:44.870
What? We know what you did.

00:30:45.980 --> 00:30:48.980
The ritual...everything.

00:30:50.420 --> 00:30:51.840
You're crazy.

00:30:51.840 --> 00:30:55.170
Your girlfriend's past her
expiration date, and we're crazy?

00:30:55.560 --> 00:30:58.300
When someone's gone,
they should stay gone.

00:30:58.300 --> 00:31:01.210
You don't mess with that kind of stuff.

00:31:01.210 --> 00:31:03.460
Angela killed matt.

00:31:03.460 --> 00:31:06.400
She tried to kill lindsay.

00:31:06.400 --> 00:31:09.680
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:31:11.810 --> 00:31:13.740
Hey,no more crap,neal!

00:31:13.740 --> 00:31:16.210
This blood is on your hands.

00:31:16.210 --> 00:31:20.060
Now,me and him can make this right,
but you got to tell us where she is.

00:31:20.950 --> 00:31:22.730
Tell us!

00:31:24.880 --> 00:31:26.850
My house.

00:31:26.850 --> 00:31:28.850
She's at my house.

00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:41.330
You sure about that?

00:31:51.010 --> 00:31:53.260
Listen. It doesn't really
matter where she is.

00:31:54.460 --> 00:31:56.990
There's only one way to stop her.

00:31:56.990 --> 00:32:01.540
We've got to perform another ritual over
her grave  to reverse the one that you did.

00:32:02.250 --> 00:32:05.490
We're going to need some black
roots, some scar weed,some candles.

00:32:05.490 --> 00:32:07.490
It's very complicated, but
it will get the job done.

00:32:07.490 --> 00:32:09.980
She'll be dead again in a couple hours.

00:32:09.980 --> 00:32:12.210
I think you should come with us.

00:32:15.600 --> 00:32:19.270
I'm serious,neal.
Leave with us right now.

00:32:19.270 --> 00:32:20.960
No.

00:32:21.720 --> 00:32:23.640
No.

00:32:28.350 --> 00:32:30.550
Listen to me.

00:32:30.550 --> 00:32:32.900
Get out of here as soon as you can.

00:32:33.960 --> 00:32:37.890
But most of all,be cool.
No sudden movements.

00:32:37.890 --> 00:32:40.860
Don't make her mad.

00:32:43.760 --> 00:32:45.270
Let's go.

00:33:01.940 --> 00:33:03.740
You said you'd stay in the house.

00:33:03.740 --> 00:33:07.100
I'm sorry. I just needed to see you.

00:33:07.380 --> 00:33:09.870
Neal,please.

00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:14.920
You have to help me.

00:33:17.620 --> 00:33:19.240
Oh,god.

00:33:19.240 --> 00:33:22.630
Come with me to the cemetery.
Neal,they're trying to kill me.

00:33:22.630 --> 00:33:24.160
We have to stop them.

00:33:24.160 --> 00:33:26.320
You mean kill them?

00:33:27.620 --> 00:33:29.610
It's
true --

00:33:29.610 --> 00:33:32.630
Matt and lindsay. They hurt me.

00:33:33.320 --> 00:33:36.420
If you love me,you'll make
sure nobody hurts me again.

00:33:36.420 --> 00:33:39.830
Take me to the cemetery,
then all this will be over.

00:33:39.830 --> 00:33:43.000
We can start new lives together.

00:33:45.090 --> 00:33:47.070
Okay.

00:33:48.330 --> 00:33:50.970
God help me,but okay.

00:33:51.760 --> 00:33:54.100
I'll go get the car.

00:33:54.100 --> 00:33:55.530
Just...

00:33:55.530 --> 00:33:57.700
Just wait here.

00:34:20.990 --> 00:34:22.980
Neal,you look nervous.

00:34:23.550 --> 00:34:25.650
No,I'm fine.

00:34:26.940 --> 00:34:29.950
Were you... going to leave me?

00:34:30.380 --> 00:34:31.940
No,of course not.

00:34:31.940 --> 00:34:34.280
You were,weren't you?!

00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:37.650
How could you?! Neal,I loved you!

00:34:37.650 --> 00:34:38.880
Angela
--

00:34:51.620 --> 00:34:54.190
You really think this is gonna work?

00:34:54.190 --> 00:34:56.770
No,not really.

00:34:58.790 --> 00:35:01.590
But it was the only thing
I could come up with.

00:35:56.850 --> 00:35:59.840
Wait. It's not what you think.

00:35:59.840 --> 00:36:03.110
I didn't ask to be brought
back, but it's still me.

00:36:03.110 --> 00:36:06.140
I'm still a person. Please.

00:36:42.090 --> 00:36:44.140
Please don't!

00:37:00.930 --> 00:37:03.470
What's dead should stay dead.

00:37:11.810 --> 00:37:13.180
Rest in peace.

00:37:13.180 --> 00:37:15.340
Yeah, for good this time,okay?

00:37:21.790 --> 00:37:23.460
You know,

00:37:23.870 --> 00:37:25.630
The whole fake-Ritual thing,

00:37:25.630 --> 00:37:29.500
Luring angela into the
cemetery -Pretty sharp.

00:37:29.500 --> 00:37:31.430
Thanks.

00:37:31.430 --> 00:37:34.010
But did we have to use me as bait?

00:37:34.010 --> 00:37:37.870
I figured you were more her type,you
know? She had pretty crappy taste in guys.

00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:40.450
I think she broke my hand.

00:37:40.950 --> 00:37:44.270
You're just too fragile.
We'll get it looked at later.

00:37:49.660 --> 00:37:51.870
You want to stay for a while?

00:37:56.580 --> 00:37:58.670
No.

00:39:06.100 --> 00:39:08.160
Dean,what is it?

00:39:12.210 --> 00:39:13.680
I'm sorry.

00:39:15.200 --> 00:39:17.160
For what?

00:39:18.890 --> 00:39:21.520
The way I've been acting.

00:39:39.350 --> 00:39:41.590
And for dad.

00:39:44.030 --> 00:39:47.180
Well, he was your dad,too.

00:39:47.970 --> 00:39:49.770
It's my fault that he's gone.

00:39:49.770 --> 00:39:51.650
What are you talking about?

00:39:51.650 --> 00:39:54.600
I know you've been
thinking it. So have I.

00:39:55.420 --> 00:39:57.960
Doesn't take a genius to figure it out.

00:39:59.340 --> 00:40:03.630
Back at the hospital,
I had a full recovery.

00:40:03.630 --> 00:40:06.410
It was a miracle.

00:40:06.410 --> 00:40:09.170
And five minutes later, dad's
dead,and the colt's gone.

00:40:09.170 --> 00:40:12.820
You can't tell me there's
not a connection there.

00:40:14.650 --> 00:40:17.690
I don't know how the demon was involved.

00:40:18.180 --> 00:40:21.680
I don't know how the whole
thing went down exactly...

00:40:22.230 --> 00:40:25.790
But dad's dead because of me.

00:40:25.790 --> 00:40:27.410
And that much I do know.

00:40:27.410 --> 00:40:29.810
We don't know that, not for sure.

00:40:29.810 --> 00:40:32.800
Sam...

00:40:34.060 --> 00:40:38.080
You and dad...

00:40:39.320 --> 00:40:42.300
You're the most important
people in my life.

00:40:42.730 --> 00:40:46.370
And now...

00:40:46.770 --> 00:40:50.340
I never should have come
back, sam. It wasn't natural.

00:40:51.830 --> 00:40:54.680
And now look what's come of it.

00:40:56.990 --> 00:40:59.250
I was dead.

00:41:00.390 --> 00:41:03.870
And I should have stayed dead.

00:41:09.490 --> 00:41:12.570
You wanted to know how I was feeling.

00:41:14.060 --> 00:41:16.830
Well,that's it.

00:41:19.300 --> 00:41:21.330
So tell me.

00:41:26.030 --> 00:41:29.620
What could you possibly
say to make that all right?



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
